    },
    {
      "id": "dghnai0",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "6. Industrial Policies in India"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "kz9iiak",
      "content": "• Industrial Policy Resolution 1948 – first industrial policy of India."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "w4chp9n",
      "content": "• Industrial Policy Resolution 1956 – emphasized public sector development."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "wqahnu9",
      "content": "• New Industrial Policy 1991 – liberalization, privatization and globalization."
    },
    {
      "id": "rdb5tes",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "7. Importance of Industries"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "82n5gfl",
      "content": "• Generates employment opportunities."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "7cnft5z",
      "content": "• Increases national income."
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Chota Nagpur Plateau region is often referred to as the 'Ruhr of India' due to its massive concentration of iron and steel industries.",
        "Understand 'Footloose Industries'—industries like IT and electronics that can be located anywhere as they are not dependent on specific raw materials.",
        "Frequently asked: The Industrial Policy Resolution of 1956 formed the basis of the Second Five-Year Plan focusing on heavy capital goods industries."
      ],
      "id": "ww7x66l"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ct6bzbq",
      "content": "• Promotes technological advancement."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "g9fzkzh",
      "content": "• Supports export growth."
    },
